{
  "name": "Steel String Guitar — Legato",
  "description": "Sample-free acoustic steel-string guitar: wgpluck2 waveguide string, velocity-sensitive pluck and brightness, finger/plectrum attack blend, and fixed wooden-body resonances. Best E2–E6. Dry centered Stereo Output; route to Master. Note-off damps the string using Release. Connected notes share one decaying string and step through equal-tempered semitones. Newest held note wins; releasing it returns to the previous held note. Gaps pluck again. Velocity and all controls are sampled at phrase start; changing a connected note's velocity does not inject another pluck. Pitch is rounded to whole semitones before pitch-synchronous transposition, with no pitch smoothing afterward. Slide defaults to a 0.12 s half-time for more distinct fret steps; this is not total slide duration.",
